media: i2c: add Hynix Hi1337 sensor driver

The Hi1337 is a 13 MP raw Bayer sensor with a 4-lane D-PHY output and a
Hi847-family register map. On the Galaxy Tab S8+ (SM-X800) it serves as
the rear main camera (4128x3096) and as the front camera (2032x1524
binned, 4000x3000 full). All three modes run at 30 fps on a 704 MHz
link (1408 Mbps per lane, pixel rate 563.2 MHz), RAW10 GRBG.

The init table and the three mode tables come from the stock SM-X800
CamX sensor modules, decoded with the vendor parameter parser. The init
table is byte-identical across the rear, front and front-full modules,
so the driver carries one copy. The tables are generated by
tools/hi1337-tables.py, which drops the mode-select writes; the driver
starts and stops the stream itself.

Power-up follows the stock sequence: vddio, vdda and vddd on, MCLK on at
19.2 MHz, 10 ms, reset released, 12 ms. Power-down asserts reset, 1 ms,
MCLK off, 1 ms, rails off. Runtime PM wraps the sequence as in hi847.

Probe reads the vendor ID at 0x0714 and the model ID at 0x0716, logs
both, and fails with -ENXIO only when the vendor ID is not 0x2000. The
CamX configuration verifies the same register and value.

Controls: link frequency, pixel rate, vblank, read-only hblank,
exposure, 8-bit analogue gain at 0x0213, digital gain across the four
Bayer channel registers (256 = 1x), and the fwnode orientation and
rotation properties.

